From 254f1e3f0703443d10e6b3dbde238094400c1d05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 1 May 2026 00:19:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/26] Subagents pill is per-TUI, scoped to the focused
 session
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

User clarification: "the intent of subagents is only to show the
subagents in that session not all subagents connected to the
server". The prior `expandedLiveSet()` aggregated direct DB
children of every focused root across all clients into a single
`subagents` array broadcast on `session.live.changed`; every TUI's
footer showed the same global count. Wrong shape.

Server simplified:
  - `LiveSessionsChanged` payload is now just `{ sessions: string[] }`
    — the deduplicated set of session IDs focused by at least one
    client. Drives the global "● N sessions" pill.
  - `expandedLiveSet()` removed entirely. `liveSessions()` returns
    the focused-IDs set directly. `_publishChange` is back to a
    plain synchronous publish (no DB lookups in the publish path).
  - `/global/live-sessions` returns `{ sessions }`.

TUI footer:
  - Sessions pill: count = `sessions.length` (was sessions.length -
    subagents.length).
  - Subagents pill: takes `sessionID` from the slot context (set by
    `routes/session/index.tsx` when rendering `session_footer`).
    Fetches `client.session.children(sessionID)` on mount and
    renders the count. Refetches when `session.created` /
    `session.deleted` events fire with `parentID === sessionID`.
    On the home route the pill renders 0 (no focus).

Tests updated: event.test.ts and event.real-server.test.ts no
longer assert on `subagents`. 8/8 still green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
